      "text": "To solve the problem, we will utilize the given functional equation and analyze the conditions that are imposed by the equation. Specifically, we have:\n\\[\nf(x) + 2f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = 3x.\n\\]\n\n### Step 1: Differentiate the Functional Equation with respect to \\( x \\)\nWe can start by differentiating both sides of the equation with respect to \\( x \\):\n\\[\nd \\left( f(x) + 2f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) \\right) = d(3x).\n\\]\nUsing the chain rule to differentiate \\( f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) \\) with respect to \\( x \\), we get:\n\\[\nd(f(x)) + 2d\\left(f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right)\\right) \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right) = 3.\n\\]\nSince \\( \\frac{d}{dx} \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = -\\frac{1}{x^2} \\), the equation becomes:\n\\[\ndf(x) - \\frac{2}{x^2} df \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = 3.\n\\]\n\nConsistently, isolate the derivative:\n\\[\ndf \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = \\frac{-(3 - x^2)}{2x^2} \\, df(x).\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Assume the Form of the Solution\nTo solve, let's assume that a linear function fits the form of \\( f(x) \\). Suppose \\( f(x) = ax + b \\). Substitute this into the original functional equation:\n\\[\na x + b + 2(a \\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right) + b) = 3x.\n\\]\nCombining the terms inside the parentheses, we obtain:\n\\[\na x + b + 2 \\left( \\frac{a}{x} + b \\right) = 3x,\n\\]\n\\[\na x + b - \\frac{2a}{x} + 2b = 3x.\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Equate Coefficients\nEquate the coefficients of the like terms:\n\\[\na = 3,\n\\]\n\\[\nb - \\frac{2a}{x} = 0.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\frac{2a}{x}\\) is independent of \\(x\\), solve for \\(b\\):\n\\[\nb = 0.\n\\]\n\nThus, the function \\(f(x) = ax + b\\) simplifies to:\n\\[\nf(x) = 3x.\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Find the Values of \\(x\\) where \\( f(x) = f(-x) \\)\nWe solve for the real solutions that satisfy \\( f(x) = f(-x) \\):\n\\[\n3x = 3(-x).\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n3x = -3x,\n\\]\n\\[\n6x = 0.\n\\]\nThus, \\(x = 0\\) does not satisfy the equation. The only value that does is when \\(x = 0\\), but it is excluded because the function is defined only for \\( x \\neq 0 \\). The solutions are thus:\n\\[\nx = -2 \\pm \\sqrt{5}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the real solutions are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2 \\pm \\sqrt{5}}.\n\\]",
